// probe_stats.hml — acceptance probe for src/sim/stats.hml and the stat-point
// budget hook in src/sim/progression.hml §7b.
//
// Run it FROM THE NIGHTSHADE REPO ROOT, both ways:
//     hemlockc -O1 tools/probe_stats.hml -o /tmp/pstats && /tmp/pstats
//     hemlock  tools/probe_stats.hml
//
// It exits 1 on any failure AND on an assertion-count mismatch.  It links no
// SDL: `nm /tmp/pstats | grep -c SDL_` must print 0.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THIS PROBE IS ACTUALLY GUARDING
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Four things, and only one of them is arithmetic:
//
//  1. **THE TRAP** (DIRECTION §9).  "Unlocks decide what you have, stats decide
//     how well you use it."  Section C sweeps every stat value, every node rank
//     and every demand tier and asserts that NOTHING is ever scaled to zero,
//     and separately that this module exports no "may I" function at all — by
//     grepping its own source for the shapes such a function would take.
//     A rule enforced only by prose is a rule that gets edited away.
//
//  2. **THE §7 GATE, IN BOTH DIRECTIONS.**  A low-Handling character must
//     genuinely fight a manufactured rifle (section B pins +45 % recoil with a
//     literal) AND must be completely unaffected on melee (pinned at exactly
//     1.0), because DIRECTION §10 says melee is the thing that always works.
//
//  3. **THE DESIGN ANCHORS, WITH LITERALS.**  CLAUDE.md rule 5: enemy caps were
//     once mutable with every probe green because every assertion was relative
//     to the config value.  SK_NEUTRAL, SK_STAT_MAX, the 29-point level-30
//     budget and the three cardinal points of the recoil curve are asserted as
//     NUMBERS.  The shapes around them are asserted as relationships.
//
//  4. **LEGIBILITY AT 320x240** (DIRECTION §9 open question 2).  Section G does
//     the layout arithmetic in the shipping font metrics instead of claiming a
//     screenshot looked fine.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THIS PROBE REFUSES TO DO
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// It does not freeze all 21 tuning coefficients as literals.  Those are meant
// to move.  What is frozen is the SHAPE: monotone, crossing 1.0 exactly at the
// neutral point, bounded away from zero, and bounded below the playability
// ceiling.  A retune that keeps the shape passes; a retune that breaks the
// support build or locks a weapon fails.

import { exit } from "@stdlib/process";
import { read_file, is_dir } from "@stdlib/fs";

